{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-yekutieli-leading-coefficient","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:yekutieli-leading-coefficient","kind":"lemma","title":"Obstruction equals the leading Chebyshev coefficient","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dq-squared","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-genus-ideal-characterisation"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-yekutieli-leading-coefficient"],"tags":["yekutieli","obstruction","chebyshev","categorical-dq-squared"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_leading_coefficient","text":"yekutieli-leading-coefficient.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:yekutieli-leading-coefficient\"></a><p>For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,p}</code> at level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = g + 1 = 5</code>, the obstruction <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(T_{2,p}) \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code> equals the leading Chebyshev coefficient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_{(p-1)/2} = 1</code>. Consequently, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(T_{2,p}) \\neq 0</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\neq 1</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/yekutieli-leading-coefficient.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"7.12.2"}
